Fail on a read error while compressing with lzop.
lzo_compress() took a negative return from full_read() as end of input.
A read error ended the output early with a valid end marker, so the
truncated .lzo file decompressed without complaint, lzop exited 0, and
-U deleted the input. Report the error and exit instead, which leaves
the input in place, as for other lzop errors.

---
 archival/lzop.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/archival/lzop.c
+++ b/archival/lzop.c
@@ -664,7 +664,9 @@
 
 		/* read a block */
 		l = full_read(0, b1, block_size);
-		src_len = (l > 0 ? l : 0);
+		if (l < 0)
+			bb_simple_perror_msg_and_die(bb_msg_read_error);
+		src_len = l;
 
 		/* write uncompressed block size */
 		/* exit if last block */
